  "caveats": [
    "Reported line values are bootstrap means; errors are the bootstrap standard deviation (upstream PyQSOFitSpec convention), not a covariance matrix.",
    "Only 10 bootstrap realisations were run, so the uncertainties are themselves noisy at the ~1/sqrt(2*(nboot-1)) level.",
    "Ugriz-type flux calibration slippage and Fe II template systematics dominate over the statistical error; the bootstrap captures neither.",
    "PyQSOFitSpec fits a single skewed profile per listed component; the Mg II 2796/2804 doublet is a single blended component, and the [O III] 5007 total is core + broad wing.",
    "Component type (broad/narrow) is assigned by the fitted sigma (log10 sigma > 0.0017 -> broad), matching QSOFit.line_prop.",
    "FWHM pinned at a sigval prior bound for MgII_na, Hb_na, OIII4959c, OIII5007c: only the flux is measured for those components (see the 'note' column of pyqsofitspec_lines.csv).",
    "unstable/multimodal components (16-84 interval > 25% of the mean): OIII4959c, OIII5007c, OIII4959w, OIII5007w; use the summed totals in pyqsofitspec_totals.csv for line-ratio work."
  ]
